{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DLANeKpBEmxJ2unxpDY3eL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Frontier architecture plan\n2\t\n3\tPlanner: Codex + GPT-5.6 Sol\n4\t\n5\tRun ID: `2026-08-23T21-56-20.470Z_codex_T7-trade-capture-plan`\n6\t\n7\tElapsed: `203.673 seconds`\n8\t\n9\tStatus: read-only pass; prompt hash matched; no workspace changes\n10\t\n11\t## Product interpretation\n12\t\n13\tThe `/trade-capture` workspace supports a local lifecycle: enter or edit a\n14\tdraft, validate and calculate economics, save or book, filter and select from\n15\ttoday's blotter, review economics, exceptions, allocations, and audit history,\n16\tthen cancel booked trades without deleting history.\n17\t\n18\tSimplifying assumptions:\n19\t\n20\t- USD only, local React state, and no external data.\n21\t- The six stable product identifiers are `agency-rmbs`, `non-agency-rmbs`,\n22\t  `cmbs`, `abs`, `clo`, and `tba-mbs`.\n23\t- Dates use ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`; timestamps use ISO strings. There is no holiday\n24\t  calendar or settlement-convention engine.\n25\t- Blank numeric form values use `null`. Calculations retain number precision\n26\t  and formatting occurs only in components.\n27\t- A missing optional client trade ID creates a warning, not an error.\n28\t- Allocation tolerance is one cent. Cancelled trades remain visible and are\n29\t  excluded from desk totals.\n30\t\n31\t## Architecture\n32\t\n33\tAdd a separate route and keep the benchmark dashboard unchanged:\n34\t\n35\t```text\n36\tapp/trade-capture/page.tsx\n37\t└── TradeCaptureApp\n38\t    ├── DeskInsights\n39\t    ├── TradeTicket\n40\t    ├── validation summary\n41\t    ├── TradeBlotter\n42\t    └── TradeReview\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\t`page.tsx` is a server route shell that imports route-specific CSS and the\n46\tclient application. `TradeCaptureApp` owns a reducer containing trades, the\n47\tticket draft, selected trade ID, filters, search, and sort. There are no server\n48\tactions, storage APIs, network calls, or database calls.\n49\t\n50\tPure domain code lives under `app/trade-capture/domain/` with no React imports.\n51\tRoute styles use `tc-` prefixed selectors below `.tc-shell` so they do not\n52\tchange the existing dashboard in `app/globals.css`.\n53\t\n54\t## Stable contracts\n55\t\n56\t```ts\n57\texport type ProductType =\n58\t  | \"agency-rmbs\"\n59\t  | \"non-agency-rmbs\"\n60\t  | \"cmbs\"\n61\t  | \"abs\"\n62\t  | \"clo\"\n63\t  | \"tba-mbs\";\n64\t\n65\texport type TradeStatus = \"draft\" | \"validated\" | \"booked\" | \"cancelled\";\n66\texport type Side = \"buy\" | \"sell\";\n67\texport type TradeModifier =\n68\t  | \"regular\"\n69\t  | \"specified-pool\"\n70\t  | \"stipulation\"\n71\t  | \"dollar-roll\"\n72\t  | \"weighted-average-price\";\n73\texport type ExceptionSeverity = \"error\" | \"warning\";\n74\t\n75\texport interface AllocationInput {\n76\t  id: string;\n77\t  label: string;\n78\t  currentFace: number | null;\n79\t}\n80\t\n81\texport interface Allocation {\n82\t  id: string;\n83\t  label: string;\n84\t  currentFace: number;\n85\t}\n86\t\n87\texport interface TradeException {\n88\t  code: string;\n89\t  severity: ExceptionSeverity;\n90\t  field: keyof TradeDraft | \"allocations\";\n91\t  message: string;\n92\t}\n93\t\n94\texport interface AuditEvent {\n95\t  id: string;\n96\t  at: string;\n97\t  action: \"created\" | \"draft-saved\" | \"validated\" | \"booked\" | \"cancelled\";\n98\t  detail: string;\n99\t}\n100\t\n101\texport interface TradeEconomics {\n102\t  currentFace: number;\n103\t  grossPrincipal: number;\n104\t  signedExposure: number;\n105\t}\n106\t\n107\texport interface TradeDraft {\n108\t  internalTradeId: string | null;\n109\t  clientTradeId: string;\n110\t  executionTimestamp: string;\n111\t  tradeDate: string;\n112\t  settlementDate: string;\n113\t  side: Side;\n114\t  productType: ProductType;\n115\t  securityId: string;\n116\t  issuerDeal: string;\n117\t  trancheClass: string;\n118\t  counterparty: string;\n119\t  book: string;\n120\t  trader: string;\n121\t  currency: \"USD\";\n122\t  originalFace: number | null;\n123\t  factor: number | null;\n124\t  price: number | null;\n125\t  coupon: number | null;\n126\t  spreadBps: number | null;\n127\t  accruedInterest: number | null;\n128\t  agency: string;\n129\t  poolNumber: string;\n130\t  weightedAverageLife: number | null;\n131\t  collateralType: string;\n132\t  rating: string;\n133\t  modifier: TradeModifier;\n134\t  allocations: AllocationInput[];\n135\t  note: string;\n136\t}\n137\t\n138\texport type Trade = Omit<TradeDraft, \"internalTradeId\" | \"allocations\"> & {\n139\t  internalTradeId: string;\n140\t  status: TradeStatus;\n141\t  allocations: Allocation[];\n142\t  economics: TradeEconomics;\n143\t  exceptions: TradeException[];\n144\t  auditEvents: AuditEvent[];\n145\t  synthetic: true;\n146\t};\n147\t\n148\texport interface DeskSummary {\n149\t  activeTradeCount: number;\n150\t  bookedTradeCount: number;\n151\t  exceptionCount: number;\n152\t  buyExposure: number;\n153\t  sellExposure: number;\n154\t  netExposure: number;\n155\t  grossPrincipal: number;\n156\t}\n157\t```\n158\t\n159\tDomain exports:\n160\t\n161\t```ts\n162\tcalculateEconomics(\n163\t  originalFace: number,\n164\t  factor: number,\n165\t  price: number,\n166\t  side: Side,\n167\t): TradeEconomics;\n168\t\n169\tvalidateTrade(draft: TradeDraft): TradeException[];\n170\t\n171\tmaterializeTrade(\n172\t  draft: TradeDraft,\n173\t  context: { id: string; status: TradeStatus; at: string },\n174\t): Trade;\n175\t\n176\tsummarizeDesk(trades: readonly Trade[]): DeskSummary;\n177\t\n178\tEMPTY_TRADE_DRAFT: Readonly<TradeDraft>;\n179\tSEED_TRADES: readonly Trade[];\n180\t```\n181\t\n182\tComponent props:\n183\t\n184\t```ts\n185\texport interface TradeTicketProps {\n186\t  draft: TradeDraft;\n187\t  exceptions: readonly TradeException[];\n188\t  onChange(next: TradeDraft): void;\n189\t  onSaveDraft(): void;\n190\t  onValidate(): void;\n191\t  onBook(): void;\n192\t  onReset(): void;\n193\t}\n194\t\n195\texport interface DeskInsightsProps {\n196\t  summary: DeskSummary;\n197\t}\n198\t\n199\texport interface TradeBlotterProps {\n200\t  trades: readonly Trade[];\n201\t  selectedTradeId: string | null;\n202\t  product: ProductType | \"all\";\n203\t  status: TradeStatus | \"all\";\n204\t  search: string;\n205\t  sort: \"execution-desc\" | \"current-face-desc\" | \"gross-principal-desc\";\n206\t  onProductChange(value: ProductType | \"all\"): void;\n207\t  onStatusChange(value: TradeStatus | \"all\"): void;\n208\t  onSearchChange(value: string): void;\n209\t  onSortChange(value: TradeBlotterProps[\"sort\"]): void;\n210\t  onSelect(id: string): void;\n211\t}\n212\t\n213\texport interface TradeReviewProps {\n214\t  trade: Trade | null;\n215\t  onEditDraft(id: string): void;\n216\t  onCancel(id: string): void;\n217\t}\n218\t```\n219\t\n220\t## File ownership\n221\t\n222\t- GPT-5.6 Terra owns:\n223\t  `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts`, `calculations.ts`, `validation.ts`,\n224\t  `seed.ts`, `index.ts`, and `tests/trade-domain.test.ts`.\n225\t- Sonnet 5 owns:\n226\t  `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx`.\n227\t- Qwen3.8-27B owns:\n228\t  `app/trade-capture/components/desk-insights.tsx`.\n229\t- Kimi K3 owns:\n230\t  `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`,\n231\t  `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`,\n232\t  `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`, and\n233\t  `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`.\n234\t- GPT-5.6 Sol integrator owns:\n235\t  `app/trade-capture/page.tsx`, `package.json`, and\n236\t  `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`.\n237\t\n238\tNo worker may modify another worker's files, existing dashboard files,\n239\tlockfiles, benchmark evidence, configuration, or integrator-owned files.\n240\t\n241\t## Worker tasks\n242\t\n243\t### Terra domain worker\n244\t\n245\tImplement every product rule, calculation, immutable seed fixtures, all-six\n246\tproduct coverage, and boundary/status tests. It may run the domain test,\n247\ttypecheck, and lint. It must not add UI or dependencies.\n248\t\n249\t### Sonnet ticket worker\n250\t\n251\tBuild a fully labelled form using semantic fieldsets, inputs, selects, inline\n252\terror associations, and real buttons. Book is disabled when errors exist. It\n253\tmust not calculate, validate, own global state, or style other panels.\n254\t\n255\t### Qwen insights worker\n256\t\n257\tRender only the supplied `DeskSummary` with clear signed and currency\n258\tformatting and meaningful headings. It must not derive totals, mutate data, or\n259\texpand into application state.\n260\t\n261\t### Kimi application worker\n262\t\n263\tImplement reducer-driven lifecycle, filtering, search, sorting, row selection,\n264\tcancellation history, review, and the responsive visual system. It consumes\n265\tdomain functions rather than duplicating rules and must not alter the ticket or\n266\tinsights components.\n267\t\n268\t## Integration sequence\n269\t\n270\t1. Apply Terra's patch and run its domain tests.\n271\t2. Freeze the domain export surface.\n272\t3. Apply Sonnet and Qwen without changing their files.\n273\t4. Apply Kimi's application and styles.\n274\t5. Add the Sol-owned route, test-script wiring, and rendered assertions.\n275\t6. Run the complete gate.\n276\t\n277\tFor an interface mismatch, record the declared contract and the worker output\n278\tthat disagree. Prefer adapting the consumer in its owning patch. If acceptance\n279\trequires an integrator edit to worker-owned code, make the smallest repair,\n280\trerun that worker's checks, and report the file and original failure. Do not\n281\tsilently normalize a patch or report it as independently passing.\n282\t\n283\t## Verification\n284\t\n285\tThe domain worker tests calculation precision, signed exposure, required\n286\tfields, numeric bounds, identifier shape, date ordering, agency and modifier\n287\trules, allocation tolerance, warnings, cancelled-trade exclusion, and seed\n288\tcoverage.\n289\t\n290\tFinal integrated gate:\n291\t\n292\t1. `node --test tests/trade-domain.test.ts`\n293\t2. `npm run typecheck`\n294\t3. `npm run lint`\n295\t4. `npm run build`\n296\t5. `node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`\n297\t6. `npm run benchmark:validate`\n298\t7. `npm run verify`\n299\t\n300\tRendered assertions request both `/` and `/trade-capture`, preserve existing\n301\tdashboard assertions, and verify the synthetic notice, totals, ticket,\n302\tvalidation region, blotter, review heading, and seed records.\n303\t\n304\tManual checks cover workflow actions, keyboard use, focus visibility, error\n305\tassociation, cancellation history, sorting, filters, search, reload reset,\n306\tconsole errors, desktop layout, and 390-pixel layout without page overflow.\n307\t\n308\t## Risks and review focus\n309\t\n310\t1. Floating-point and blank-number handling could violate precise calculations\n311\t   or allocation tolerance.\n312\t2. Product/modifier validation and lifecycle transitions could diverge between\n313\t   domain code and reducer logic.\n314\t3. Seed data could accidentally resemble real clients, traders, accounts, or\n315\t   regulated records.\n316\t4. Cross-worker contract or CSS drift could yield a type-correct but inaccessible\n317\t   UI.\n318\t5. Hydration, timestamps, responsive tables, or route styles could break\n319\t   rendered HTML, mobile usability, or the existing dashboard.\n320\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0534d7a-1d7b-4a4f-b438-f153dd9a57ff","uuid":"298efe9a-f7fc-44b2-92ca-7b8b64fe940f","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:01:35.659Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-o2LLK6/checkout/benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md","content":"# Frontier architecture plan\n\nPlanner: Codex + GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nRun ID: `2026-08-23T21-56-20.470Z_codex_T7-trade-capture-plan`\n\nElapsed: `203.673 seconds`\n\nStatus: read-only pass; prompt hash matched; no workspace changes\n\n## Product interpretation\n\nThe `/trade-capture` workspace supports a local lifecycle: enter or edit a\ndraft, validate and calculate economics, save or book, filter and select from\ntoday's blotter, review economics, exceptions, allocations, and audit history,\nthen cancel booked trades without deleting history.\n\nSimplifying assumptions:\n\n- USD only, local React state, and no external data.\n- The six stable product identifiers are `agency-rmbs`, `non-agency-rmbs`,\n  `cmbs`, `abs`, `clo`, and `tba-mbs`.\n- Dates use ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`; timestamps use ISO strings. There is no holiday\n  calendar or settlement-convention engine.\n- Blank numeric form values use `null`. Calculations retain number precision\n  and formatting occurs only in components.\n- A missing optional client trade ID creates a warning, not an error.\n- Allocation tolerance is one cent. Cancelled trades remain visible and are\n  excluded from desk totals.\n\n## Architecture\n\nAdd a separate route and keep the benchmark dashboard unchanged:\n\n```text\napp/trade-capture/page.tsx\n└── TradeCaptureApp\n    ├── DeskInsights\n    ├── TradeTicket\n    ├── validation summary\n    ├── TradeBlotter\n    └── TradeReview\n```\n\n`page.tsx` is a server route shell that imports route-specific CSS and the\nclient application. `TradeCaptureApp` owns a reducer containing trades, the\nticket draft, selected trade ID, filters, search, and sort. There are no server\nactions, storage APIs, network calls, or database calls.\n\nPure domain code lives under `app/trade-capture/domain/` with no React imports.\nRoute styles use `tc-` prefixed selectors below `.tc-shell` so they do not\nchange the existing dashboard in `app/globals.css`.\n\n## Stable contracts\n\n```ts\nexport type ProductType =\n  | \"agency-rmbs\"\n  | \"non-agency-rmbs\"\n  | \"cmbs\"\n  | \"abs\"\n  | \"clo\"\n  | \"tba-mbs\";\n\nexport type TradeStatus = \"draft\" | \"validated\" | \"booked\" | \"cancelled\";\nexport type Side = \"buy\" | \"sell\";\nexport type TradeModifier =\n  | \"regular\"\n  | \"specified-pool\"\n  | \"stipulation\"\n  | \"dollar-roll\"\n  | \"weighted-average-price\";\nexport type ExceptionSeverity = \"error\" | \"warning\";\n\nexport interface AllocationInput {\n  id: string;\n  label: string;\n  currentFace: number | null;\n}\n\nexport interface Allocation {\n  id: string;\n  label: string;\n  currentFace: number;\n}\n\nexport interface TradeException {\n  code: string;\n  severity: ExceptionSeverity;\n  field: keyof TradeDraft | \"allocations\";\n  message: string;\n}\n\nexport interface AuditEvent {\n  id: string;\n  at: string;\n  action: \"created\" | \"draft-saved\" | \"validated\" | \"booked\" | \"cancelled\";\n  detail: string;\n}\n\nexport interface TradeEconomics {\n  currentFace: number;\n  grossPrincipal: number;\n  signedExposure: number;\n}\n\nexport interface TradeDraft {\n  internalTradeId: string | null;\n  clientTradeId: string;\n  executionTimestamp: string;\n  tradeDate: string;\n  settlementDate: string;\n  side: Side;\n  productType: ProductType;\n  securityId: string;\n  issuerDeal: string;\n  trancheClass: string;\n  counterparty: string;\n  book: string;\n  trader: string;\n  currency: \"USD\";\n  originalFace: number | null;\n  factor: number | null;\n  price: number | null;\n  coupon: number | null;\n  spreadBps: number | null;\n  accruedInterest: number | null;\n  agency: string;\n  poolNumber: string;\n  weightedAverageLife: number | null;\n  collateralType: string;\n  rating: string;\n  modifier: TradeModifier;\n  allocations: AllocationInput[];\n  note: string;\n}\n\nexport type Trade = Omit<TradeDraft, \"internalTradeId\" | \"allocations\"> & {\n  internalTradeId: string;\n  status: TradeStatus;\n  allocations: Allocation[];\n  economics: TradeEconomics;\n  exceptions: TradeException[];\n  auditEvents: AuditEvent[];\n  synthetic: true;\n};\n\nexport interface DeskSummary {\n  activeTradeCount: number;\n  bookedTradeCount: number;\n  exceptionCount: number;\n  buyExposure: number;\n  sellExposure: number;\n  netExposure: number;\n  grossPrincipal: number;\n}\n```\n\nDomain exports:\n\n```ts\ncalculateEconomics(\n  originalFace: number,\n  factor: number,\n  price: number,\n  side: Side,\n): TradeEconomics;\n\nvalidateTrade(draft: TradeDraft): TradeException[];\n\nmaterializeTrade(\n  draft: TradeDraft,\n  context: { id: string; status: TradeStatus; at: string },\n): Trade;\n\nsummarizeDesk(trades: readonly Trade[]): DeskSummary;\n\nEMPTY_TRADE_DRAFT: Readonly<TradeDraft>;\nSEED_TRADES: readonly Trade[];\n```\n\nComponent props:\n\n```ts\nexport interface TradeTicketProps {\n  draft: TradeDraft;\n  exceptions: readonly TradeException[];\n  onChange(next: TradeDraft): void;\n  onSaveDraft(): void;\n  onValidate(): void;\n  onBook(): void;\n  onReset(): void;\n}\n\nexport interface DeskInsightsProps {\n  summary: DeskSummary;\n}\n\nexport interface TradeBlotterProps {\n  trades: readonly Trade[];\n  selectedTradeId: string | null;\n  product: ProductType | \"all\";\n  status: TradeStatus | \"all\";\n  search: string;\n  sort: \"execution-desc\" | \"current-face-desc\" | \"gross-principal-desc\";\n  onProductChange(value: ProductType | \"all\"): void;\n  onStatusChange(value: TradeStatus | \"all\"): void;\n  onSearchChange(value: string): void;\n  onSortChange(value: TradeBlotterProps[\"sort\"]): void;\n  onSelect(id: string): void;\n}\n\nexport interface TradeReviewProps {\n  trade: Trade | null;\n  onEditDraft(id: string): void;\n  onCancel(id: string): void;\n}\n```\n\n## File ownership\n\n- GPT-5.6 Terra owns:\n  `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts`, `calculations.ts`, `validation.ts`,\n  `seed.ts`, `index.ts`, and `tests/trade-domain.test.ts`.\n- Sonnet 5 owns:\n  `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx`.\n- Qwen3.8-27B owns:\n  `app/trade-capture/components/desk-insights.tsx`.\n- Kimi K3 owns:\n  `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`,\n  `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`,\n  `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`, and\n  `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`.\n- GPT-5.6 Sol integrator owns:\n  `app/trade-capture/page.tsx`, `package.json`, and\n  `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`.\n\nNo worker may modify another worker's files, existing dashboard files,\nlockfiles, benchmark evidence, configuration, or integrator-owned files.\n\n## Worker tasks\n\n### Terra domain worker\n\nImplement every product rule, calculation, immutable seed fixtures, all-six\nproduct coverage, and boundary/status tests. It may run the domain test,\ntypecheck, and lint. It must not add UI or dependencies.\n\n### Sonnet ticket worker\n\nBuild a fully labelled form using semantic fieldsets, inputs, selects, inline\nerror associations, and real buttons. Book is disabled when errors exist. It\nmust not calculate, validate, own global state, or style other panels.\n\n### Qwen insights worker\n\nRender only the supplied `DeskSummary` with clear signed and currency\nformatting and meaningful headings. It must not derive totals, mutate data, or\nexpand into application state.\n\n### Kimi application worker\n\nImplement reducer-driven lifecycle, filtering, search, sorting, row selection,\ncancellation history, review, and the responsive visual system. It consumes\ndomain functions rather than duplicating rules and must not alter the ticket or\ninsights components.\n\n## Integration sequence\n\n1. Apply Terra's patch and run its domain tests.\n2. Freeze the domain export surface.\n3. Apply Sonnet and Qwen without changing their files.\n4. Apply Kimi's application and styles.\n5. Add the Sol-owned route, test-script wiring, and rendered assertions.\n6. Run the complete gate.\n\nFor an interface mismatch, record the declared contract and the worker output\nthat disagree. Prefer adapting the consumer in its owning patch. If acceptance\nrequires an integrator edit to worker-owned code, make the smallest repair,\nrerun that worker's checks, and report the file and original failure. Do not\nsilently normalize a patch or report it as independently passing.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe domain worker tests calculation precision, signed exposure, required\nfields, numeric bounds, identifier shape, date ordering, agency and modifier\nrules, allocation tolerance, warnings, cancelled-trade exclusion, and seed\ncoverage.\n\nFinal integrated gate:\n\n1. `node --test tests/trade-domain.test.ts`\n2. `npm run typecheck`\n3. `npm run lint`\n4. `npm run build`\n5. `node --test tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`\n6. `npm run benchmark:validate`\n7. `npm run verify`\n\nRendered assertions request both `/` and `/trade-capture`, preserve existing\ndashboard assertions, and verify the synthetic notice, totals, ticket,\nvalidation region, blotter, review heading, and seed records.\n\nManual checks cover workflow actions, keyboard use, focus visibility, error\nassociation, cancellation history, sorting, filters, search, reload reset,\nconsole errors, desktop layout, and 390-pixel layout without page overflow.\n\n## Risks and review focus\n\n1. Floating-point and blank-number handling could violate precise calculations\n   or allocation tolerance.\n2. Product/modifier validation and lifecycle transitions could diverge between\n   domain code and reducer logic.\n3. Seed data could accidentally resemble real clients, traders, accounts, or\n   regulated records.\n4. Cross-worker contract or CSS drift could yield a type-correct but inaccessible\n   UI.\n5. Hydration, timestamps, responsive tables, or route styles could break\n   rendered HTML, mobile usability, or the existing dashboard.\n","numLines":320,"startLine":1,"totalLines":320}}}
