{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159hUggLXwa9VZUJWLiZ4aj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Frontier architecture review\n2\t\n3\tReviewer: Claude Code + Opus 5\n4\t\n5\tRun ID: `2026-08-23T22-01-06.339Z_claude_T7-trade-capture-plan-review`\n6\t\n7\tElapsed: `319.008 seconds`\n8\t\n9\tVerdict: **approve with required changes**\n10\t\n11\tStatus: read-only pass; prompt hash matched; no workspace changes or permission\n12\tdenials\n13\t\n14\t## Required changes accepted\n15\t\n16\t1. Replace the single materialization function with explicit draft, validate,\n17\t   book, and cancel lifecycle functions that preserve identity and audit history.\n18\t2. Add `editingTradeId` to application state and prevent cancelled-trade edits.\n19\t3. Freeze signed exposure and every desk-summary calculation.\n20\t4. Use `tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`, explicit `.ts` imports, `import type`, and\n21\t   `allowImportingTsExtensions` so Node and TypeScript agree.\n22\t5. Include the domain test in the ordinary `npm test` gate.\n23\t6. Keep worker verification to domain tests, typecheck, and lint; do not require\n24\t   network-sensitive builds inside worker stages.\n25\t7. Put reducer transitions and blotter selectors in pure importable modules so\n26\t   they can be tested without a browser.\n27\t8. Freeze exception codes and form-field IDs for reliable error association.\n28\t9. Keep allocations read-only in the first mock. Seed trades may contain them;\n29\t   newly entered trades may use an empty allocation list.\n30\t10. Add an integer-cent comparison helper for allocation totals.\n31\t11. Make seed timestamps and empty-draft values deterministic. Generate new IDs\n32\t    and audit times only inside event handling.\n33\t12. Require every route stylesheet selector to begin with `.tc-`.\n34\t13. Freeze a minimum accessible table, row-selection, validation-region, and\n35\t    disabled-book reason contract.\n36\t14. Establish two worker baselines: B1 contains stable types and compiling\n37\t    stubs; Terra replaces the domain stubs, and its accepted result becomes B2.\n38\t    Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi then start independently from B2.\n39\t\n40\t## Calculation definitions\n41\t\n42\t- `signedExposure = buy ? grossPrincipal : -grossPrincipal`.\n43\t- `buyExposure` is the sum of positive signed exposure.\n44\t- `sellExposure` is the sum of negative signed exposure and remains negative.\n45\t- `netExposure = buyExposure + sellExposure`.\n46\t- Desk `grossPrincipal` is the sum of absolute signed exposure.\n47\t- Active count excludes cancelled trades.\n48\t- Booked count includes only booked trades.\n49\t- Exception count includes error-severity exceptions on non-cancelled trades.\n50\t\n51\t## State and component clarifications\n52\t\n53\t- Live validation recomputes on every ticket change.\n54\t- Validate also writes a validated record and appends an audit event.\n55\t- Book always revalidates before committing.\n56\t- The blotter receives the full trade collection and applies the pure shared\n57\t  selector internally.\n58\t- After cancelling a selected trade, selection remains on that preserved record\n59\t  and focus returns to the review heading.\n60\t- Row selection uses a real button with `aria-pressed`, not a clickable row.\n61\t- The blotter uses a caption and a labelled focusable scroll region.\n62\t- Validation uses a `role=\"status\"` live region.\n63\t- Book uses the native disabled state plus a visible reason.\n64\t\n65\t## Worker baseline correction\n66\t\n67\tB1 must contain stable types, route composition, package/TypeScript test wiring,\n68\tand compiling stubs for every worker-owned file. Terra starts from B1. Its\n69\taccepted patch is integrated and committed as B2. Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi then\n70\tstart from B2, so their imports resolve while their file ownership remains\n71\tnon-overlapping.\n72\t\n73\t## Verification additions\n74\t\n75\t- lifecycle and illegal-transition tests;\n76\t- audit preservation across edit, book, and cancel;\n77\t- deterministic filter, search, sort, and tie-breaking tests;\n78\t- seed exceptions generated from current validation;\n79\t- cancelled trades excluded from summary totals;\n80\t- route assertions for labels, described errors, status region, caption, and\n81\t  synthetic notice;\n82\t- negative assertion that the benchmark homepage contains no `tc-` markup; and\n83\t- later manual checks for interaction, focus, console, reload reset, desktop,\n84\t  and 390-pixel layout.\n85\t\n86\t## Telemetry note\n87\t\n88\tClaude Code reported `$1.2314075` of subscription CLI telemetry. Anthropic usage\n89\tcredits were not enabled, so it is not counted as metered project spend.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0534d7a-1d7b-4a4f-b438-f153dd9a57ff","uuid":"85862610-a7fc-47d3-839b-033a25185d56","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:01:36.167Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-o2LLK6/checkout/benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/ARCHITECTURE-OPUS-REVIEW.md","content":"# Frontier architecture review\n\nReviewer: Claude Code + Opus 5\n\nRun ID: `2026-08-23T22-01-06.339Z_claude_T7-trade-capture-plan-review`\n\nElapsed: `319.008 seconds`\n\nVerdict: **approve with required changes**\n\nStatus: read-only pass; prompt hash matched; no workspace changes or permission\ndenials\n\n## Required changes accepted\n\n1. Replace the single materialization function with explicit draft, validate,\n   book, and cancel lifecycle functions that preserve identity and audit history.\n2. Add `editingTradeId` to application state and prevent cancelled-trade edits.\n3. Freeze signed exposure and every desk-summary calculation.\n4. Use `tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`, explicit `.ts` imports, `import type`, and\n   `allowImportingTsExtensions` so Node and TypeScript agree.\n5. Include the domain test in the ordinary `npm test` gate.\n6. Keep worker verification to domain tests, typecheck, and lint; do not require\n   network-sensitive builds inside worker stages.\n7. Put reducer transitions and blotter selectors in pure importable modules so\n   they can be tested without a browser.\n8. Freeze exception codes and form-field IDs for reliable error association.\n9. Keep allocations read-only in the first mock. Seed trades may contain them;\n   newly entered trades may use an empty allocation list.\n10. Add an integer-cent comparison helper for allocation totals.\n11. Make seed timestamps and empty-draft values deterministic. Generate new IDs\n    and audit times only inside event handling.\n12. Require every route stylesheet selector to begin with `.tc-`.\n13. Freeze a minimum accessible table, row-selection, validation-region, and\n    disabled-book reason contract.\n14. Establish two worker baselines: B1 contains stable types and compiling\n    stubs; Terra replaces the domain stubs, and its accepted result becomes B2.\n    Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi then start independently from B2.\n\n## Calculation definitions\n\n- `signedExposure = buy ? grossPrincipal : -grossPrincipal`.\n- `buyExposure` is the sum of positive signed exposure.\n- `sellExposure` is the sum of negative signed exposure and remains negative.\n- `netExposure = buyExposure + sellExposure`.\n- Desk `grossPrincipal` is the sum of absolute signed exposure.\n- Active count excludes cancelled trades.\n- Booked count includes only booked trades.\n- Exception count includes error-severity exceptions on non-cancelled trades.\n\n## State and component clarifications\n\n- Live validation recomputes on every ticket change.\n- Validate also writes a validated record and appends an audit event.\n- Book always revalidates before committing.\n- The blotter receives the full trade collection and applies the pure shared\n  selector internally.\n- After cancelling a selected trade, selection remains on that preserved record\n  and focus returns to the review heading.\n- Row selection uses a real button with `aria-pressed`, not a clickable row.\n- The blotter uses a caption and a labelled focusable scroll region.\n- Validation uses a `role=\"status\"` live region.\n- Book uses the native disabled state plus a visible reason.\n\n## Worker baseline correction\n\nB1 must contain stable types, route composition, package/TypeScript test wiring,\nand compiling stubs for every worker-owned file. Terra starts from B1. Its\naccepted patch is integrated and committed as B2. Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi then\nstart from B2, so their imports resolve while their file ownership remains\nnon-overlapping.\n\n## Verification additions\n\n- lifecycle and illegal-transition tests;\n- audit preservation across edit, book, and cancel;\n- deterministic filter, search, sort, and tie-breaking tests;\n- seed exceptions generated from current validation;\n- cancelled trades excluded from summary totals;\n- route assertions for labels, described errors, status region, caption, and\n  synthetic notice;\n- negative assertion that the benchmark homepage contains no `tc-` markup; and\n- later manual checks for interaction, focus, console, reload reset, desktop,\n  and 390-pixel layout.\n\n## Telemetry note\n\nClaude Code reported `$1.2314075` of subscription CLI telemetry. Anthropic usage\ncredits were not enabled, so it is not counted as metered project spend.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
