{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AZFKHhPPgX4H6HkFCFiRYm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Frozen distributed implementation contract\n2\t\n3\tContract version: `1.0.0`\n4\t\n5\tThis file incorporates the required changes from the Sol plan and Opus review.\n6\tWorker prompts may narrow it but may not contradict it.\n7\t\n8\t## Baselines\n9\t\n10\t- **B1:** stable types, route, package and TypeScript wiring, rendered assertions,\n11\t  and compiling worker stubs.\n12\t- **B2:** B1 plus the accepted Terra domain implementation and domain tests.\n13\t- Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi each start from B2 in fresh isolated worktrees.\n14\t\n15\t## Stable domain behavior\n16\t\n17\t- Calculations and validation live only in the domain layer.\n18\t- Lifecycle helpers preserve the internal ID and append audit history.\n19\t- Booking revalidates and throws while any error exists.\n20\t- Cancellation throws unless the record is booked.\n21\t- Cancelled records remain visible but do not contribute to summary totals.\n22\t- `signedExposure` uses gross principal: buys positive, sells negative.\n23\t- Sell exposure stays negative in `DeskSummary`.\n24\t- Allocation difference uses rounded integer cents with a tolerance of one cent.\n25\t- Allocations are read-only in the first mock. Seed trades may contain them;\n26\t  new tickets use an empty list.\n27\t- Empty-draft and seed timestamps are fixed strings. IDs and audit timestamps\n28\t  are created only inside explicit state actions.\n29\t\n30\t## Stable state behavior\n31\t\n32\t- State owns trades, draft, live exceptions, `editingTradeId`, selection,\n33\t  product/status filters, search, and sort.\n34\t- Reducer actions are `draft-changed`, `reset`, `save-draft`, `validate`,\n35\t  `book`, `edit`, `cancel`, `selected`, `product-filtered`,\n36\t  `status-filtered`, `searched`, and `sorted`. Lifecycle actions receive a\n37\t  caller-created `{ id, at }` context so the reducer itself stays deterministic.\n38\t- Editing loads the selected non-cancelled trade and preserves its ID/history.\n39\t- Reset clears `editingTradeId` and restores the deterministic empty draft.\n40\t- Validate writes a validated record. Book revalidates and writes a booked\n41\t  record. Cancel preserves selection on the cancelled record.\n42\t- Reducer and selectors have no React import and are independently testable.\n43\t- Search covers internal ID, client trade ID, security ID, issuer/deal, and\n44\t  counterparty, case-insensitively.\n45\t- Sort order is stable and uses internal trade ID as the final tie-breaker.\n46\t\n47\t## Stable accessibility behavior\n48\t\n49\t- Ticket controls use `tc-field-{field}` IDs.\n50\t- Error messages use `tc-error-{field}` IDs.\n51\t- Error controls set `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`.\n52\t- Validation summary uses `role=\"status\"` and live updates.\n53\t- Book is disabled while errors exist and shows a visible explanation.\n54\t- Blotter is a semantic table with a caption.\n55\t- The scroll wrapper is focusable, has `role=\"region\"`, and has an accessible\n56\t  name.\n57\t- Each row has a selection button with `aria-pressed`.\n58\t- Route CSS contains no bare element selector, `:root`, or universal selector;\n59\t  every selector begins with `.tc-`.\n60\t\n61\t## Stable exception ownership\n62\t\n63\tException codes are frozen in `domain/types.ts`. Cross-field failures attach to:\n64\t\n65\t- settlement ordering → `settlementDate`;\n66\t- modifier/product conflicts → `modifier`;\n67\t- agency requirement → `agency`;\n68\t- specified pool requirement → `poolNumber`;\n69\t- allocation mismatch → `allocations`.\n70\t\n71\t## Stable file ownership\n72\t\n73\t### Terra\n74\t\n75\t- `app/trade-capture/domain/calculations.ts`\n76\t- `app/trade-capture/domain/validation.ts`\n77\t- `app/trade-capture/domain/lifecycle.ts`\n78\t- `app/trade-capture/domain/seed.ts`\n79\t- `tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`\n80\t\n81\t### Sonnet\n82\t\n83\t- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx`\n84\t\n85\t### Qwen\n86\t\n87\t- `app/trade-capture/components/desk-insights.tsx`\n88\t\n89\t### Kimi\n90\t\n91\t- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`\n92\t- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`\n93\t- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`\n94\t- `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts`\n95\t- `app/trade-capture/state/selectors.ts`\n96\t- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`\n97\t\n98\t### Sol integrator\n99\t\n100\t- `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts`\n101\t- `app/trade-capture/domain/index.ts`\n102\t- `app/trade-capture/page.tsx`\n103\t- `package.json`\n104\t- `tsconfig.json`\n105\t- `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`\n106\t\n107\tNo implementation worker may change an integrator file or another worker's\n108\tfile. Sol records every later repair to worker-owned code.\n109\t\n110\t## Worker verification\n111\t\n112\t- Terra: `node --test tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`, `npm run typecheck`, and\n113\t  `npm run lint`.\n114\t- Sonnet, Qwen, Kimi: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`.\n115\t- No worker runs a build or uses the network.\n116\t- Final Sol integration runs the complete repository gate.\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0534d7a-1d7b-4a4f-b438-f153dd9a57ff","uuid":"2b3eb03a-abce-412c-808c-e494b88a5584","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:01:40.007Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-o2LLK6/checkout/benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/CONTRACT.md","content":"# Frozen distributed implementation contract\n\nContract version: `1.0.0`\n\nThis file incorporates the required changes from the Sol plan and Opus review.\nWorker prompts may narrow it but may not contradict it.\n\n## Baselines\n\n- **B1:** stable types, route, package and TypeScript wiring, rendered assertions,\n  and compiling worker stubs.\n- **B2:** B1 plus the accepted Terra domain implementation and domain tests.\n- Sonnet, Qwen, and Kimi each start from B2 in fresh isolated worktrees.\n\n## Stable domain behavior\n\n- Calculations and validation live only in the domain layer.\n- Lifecycle helpers preserve the internal ID and append audit history.\n- Booking revalidates and throws while any error exists.\n- Cancellation throws unless the record is booked.\n- Cancelled records remain visible but do not contribute to summary totals.\n- `signedExposure` uses gross principal: buys positive, sells negative.\n- Sell exposure stays negative in `DeskSummary`.\n- Allocation difference uses rounded integer cents with a tolerance of one cent.\n- Allocations are read-only in the first mock. Seed trades may contain them;\n  new tickets use an empty list.\n- Empty-draft and seed timestamps are fixed strings. IDs and audit timestamps\n  are created only inside explicit state actions.\n\n## Stable state behavior\n\n- State owns trades, draft, live exceptions, `editingTradeId`, selection,\n  product/status filters, search, and sort.\n- Reducer actions are `draft-changed`, `reset`, `save-draft`, `validate`,\n  `book`, `edit`, `cancel`, `selected`, `product-filtered`,\n  `status-filtered`, `searched`, and `sorted`. Lifecycle actions receive a\n  caller-created `{ id, at }` context so the reducer itself stays deterministic.\n- Editing loads the selected non-cancelled trade and preserves its ID/history.\n- Reset clears `editingTradeId` and restores the deterministic empty draft.\n- Validate writes a validated record. Book revalidates and writes a booked\n  record. Cancel preserves selection on the cancelled record.\n- Reducer and selectors have no React import and are independently testable.\n- Search covers internal ID, client trade ID, security ID, issuer/deal, and\n  counterparty, case-insensitively.\n- Sort order is stable and uses internal trade ID as the final tie-breaker.\n\n## Stable accessibility behavior\n\n- Ticket controls use `tc-field-{field}` IDs.\n- Error messages use `tc-error-{field}` IDs.\n- Error controls set `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`.\n- Validation summary uses `role=\"status\"` and live updates.\n- Book is disabled while errors exist and shows a visible explanation.\n- Blotter is a semantic table with a caption.\n- The scroll wrapper is focusable, has `role=\"region\"`, and has an accessible\n  name.\n- Each row has a selection button with `aria-pressed`.\n- Route CSS contains no bare element selector, `:root`, or universal selector;\n  every selector begins with `.tc-`.\n\n## Stable exception ownership\n\nException codes are frozen in `domain/types.ts`. Cross-field failures attach to:\n\n- settlement ordering → `settlementDate`;\n- modifier/product conflicts → `modifier`;\n- agency requirement → `agency`;\n- specified pool requirement → `poolNumber`;\n- allocation mismatch → `allocations`.\n\n## Stable file ownership\n\n### Terra\n\n- `app/trade-capture/domain/calculations.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/domain/validation.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/domain/lifecycle.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/domain/seed.ts`\n- `tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`\n\n### Sonnet\n\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx`\n\n### Qwen\n\n- `app/trade-capture/components/desk-insights.tsx`\n\n### Kimi\n\n- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-blotter.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx`\n- `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/state/selectors.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css`\n\n### Sol integrator\n\n- `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/domain/index.ts`\n- `app/trade-capture/page.tsx`\n- `package.json`\n- `tsconfig.json`\n- `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs`\n\nNo implementation worker may change an integrator file or another worker's\nfile. Sol records every later repair to worker-owned code.\n\n## Worker verification\n\n- Terra: `node --test tests/trade-domain.test.mjs`, `npm run typecheck`, and\n  `npm run lint`.\n- Sonnet, Qwen, Kimi: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint`.\n- No worker runs a build or uses the network.\n- Final Sol integration runs the complete repository gate.\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}}}
