{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeLg8Kb9mWi8UX5yUjpZb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pb33zxa2fB8PGwx5PU4WYA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ammarbinayaz/.claude/plans/independent-final-review-sharded-octopus.md","content":"# Context\n\nIndependent final review of the completed T7 securitized-product trade-capture\nmock at `/trade-capture`. This is a read-only evidence review: no files were\nedited, no commands run, no network access, and `benchmark/private` and\n`benchmark/runs` were not read. The deliverable is the review below, not a code\nchange. Sources read: `PRODUCT.md`, `ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md`,\n`ARCHITECTURE-OPUS-REVIEW.md`, `CONTRACT.md`, `DECISIONS.md`,\n`IMPLEMENTATION-LOG.md`, all 15 files under `app/trade-capture`, the three\nsuites under `tests`, plus `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, and `app/layout.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\n`ACCEPT WITH FINDINGS` — the mock implements the frozen domain, state, and\naccessibility contracts faithfully and the implementation log is honest about\nmodel output, fallback, cost, and unverified browser QA, but the lifecycle\nallows a booked trade to regress to draft, and the validate/book actions clear\nthe ticket in a way that makes the intended capture flow confusing.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **high** — `app/trade-capture/domain/lifecycle.ts:37-43`,\n   `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts:120-137`. Booked records can silently\n   regress. `edit` accepts any non-cancelled trade, and `saveDraft` /\n   `validateTradeRecord` accept any `existing` trade and unconditionally write\n   `status: \"draft\"` / `\"validated\"`. Editing a booked trade and pressing Save\n   draft moves it back to `draft`, removes it from `bookedTradeCount`\n   (`calculations.ts:34`), and makes it permanently uncancellable\n   (`lifecycle.ts:53-56`). Only two transitions are guarded (book-with-errors,\n   cancel-non-booked) and no test covers the downgrade path.\n\n2. **high** — `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts:82-96` with\n   `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx:48-62`. `storeTrade` resets\n   `draft` to `emptyDraft()` and `editingTradeId` to `null` after `save-draft`,\n   `validate`, and `book`. Consequences: (a) the natural\n   fill → Validate → Book path is impossible, since Validate empties the ticket\n   and re-disables Book, forcing the user through blotter select → \"Edit in\n   ticket\"; (b) immediately after a successful Book the `role=\"status\"` region\n   flips to `Ticket needs attention` with 8 errors, because the freshly emptied\n   draft fails validation. Success is announced as failure to screen readers.\n\n3. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx:25-51`,\n   `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx:73,99,137`. No touched/dirty\n   tracking. `INITIAL_STATE.exceptions = validateTrade(initialDraft)`\n   (`reducer.ts:103`) means first paint of an untouched ticket shows a red\n   \"Ticket needs attention\" banner and sets `aria-invalid=\"true\"` plus inline\n   error text on eight fields the user has never visited. Live validation on\n   every change is contract-required, but validating a pristine form is not.\n\n4. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/domain/validation.ts:39-41`,\n   `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts:26-41`. `PRODUCT.md` rule 1 makes trade\n   date and settlement date required, but no `required-trade-date` /\n   `required-settlement-date` code exists and the only date rule is the ordering\n   check, which is skipped when either value is empty. Both fields are clearable\n   `type=\"date\"` inputs (`trade-ticket.tsx:215-230`), so a trade with no trade\n   date books cleanly.\n\n5. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx:104-109`;\n   confirmed absent across the route (no `useRef`, `useEffect`, or `.focus(`\n   anywhere under `app/trade-capture`). `ARCHITECTURE-OPUS-REVIEW.md:60-61`\n   requires focus to return to the review heading after cancelling. Instead the\n   activated \"Cancel trade\" button becomes `disabled`, so focus drops to\n   `<body>`. \"Edit in ticket\" likewise moves no focus, which matters at 390px\n   where the ticket sits above the review panel and the population is off-screen.\n\n6. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts:133-141`,\n   `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx:54-62`. `editingTradeId` never\n   reaches the UI: `TradeTicketProps` has no editing field and the ticket\n   heading always reads \"New trade\". Selection and editing can diverge — select\n   trade A, press \"Edit in ticket\", then click trade B's row — after which Book\n   overwrites A while the review panel shows B, with no visible cue.\n\n7. **medium** — `tests/trade-workspace.test.mjs`,\n   `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:54-75`. The frozen accessibility contract\n   (`CONTRACT.md:48-59`) is almost entirely unasserted: no test checks\n   `aria-describedby`/`aria-invalid` error association, `aria-pressed` on row\n   buttons, the labelled focusable scroll region, or the disabled-Book reason;\n   `ARCHITECTURE-OPUS-REVIEW.md:77-82` explicitly asked for \"described errors\"\n   assertions. State coverage also omits `reset`, `save-draft` on an existing\n   trade, the cancelled-trade edit guard, and the internal-ID tie-breaker (the\n   sort test only re-sorts the output it received). No component-level render\n   test exists; page checks are regex over server HTML.\n\n8. **low** — `benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/IMPLEMENTATION-LOG.md:139-146`.\n   The declared final gate in `ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md:290-298` ends with\n   `npm run verify`, which additionally runs `benchmark:mcp:test`. The log\n   reports typecheck, lint, `npm test`, `benchmark:validate`, and\n   `git diff --check`, but not `npm run verify`. The \"11 public\n   behavior/render checks\" count does match the suites (2 + 6 + 3).\n\n9. **low** — `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css:654-666,830-900`. The blotter\n   table is pinned to `min-width: 1120px`, so at 390px all nine columns are\n   reachable only by horizontal scrolling inside the region, with no stacked\n   fallback. Separately `.tc-shell { overflow-x: clip }` (line 18) suppresses\n   page-level overflow rather than preventing it, so a future overflow\n   regression would be hidden from exactly the manual 390px check that is\n   supposed to catch it.\n\n10. **low** — `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css:10,216-221,507-511,540-544`.\n    `--tc-muted` (#68777b) on the #f2f5f1/#fffdf8 panels computes to roughly\n    4.2:1, under the 4.5:1 AA threshold for normal text, and it is applied at\n    8–11px (`.tc-exception strong` 8px, `.tc-detail-grid dt` 9px,\n    `.tc-audit-list span` 9px). Contrast is calculated from the source values,\n    not measured in a browser.\n\n11. **low** — `package.json:5-12`, `tsconfig.json`. `npm test` imports `.ts`\n    modules from `.mjs` suites, which needs unflagged type stripping (Node\n    ≥22.18), while `engines.node` allows `>=22.13.0`. `erasableSyntaxOnly` is\n    not set, so a future `enum` or parameter property in the domain would pass\n    typecheck and break the domain suite at runtime.\n\n## Contract coverage\n\n- Six stable product identifiers, all trade fields, and the `TradeDraft` /\n  `Trade` / `DeskSummary` shapes match `ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md` (`domain/types.ts`).\n- `current face = original face × factor`, `gross principal = current face ×\n  price / 100`, signed exposure, and desk totals excluding cancelled trades\n  (`domain/calculations.ts`), with `sellExposure` kept negative.\n- Validation rules 2–4 and 6–11, exception-code freeze, and cross-field\n  ownership (settlement→`settlementDate`, modifier→`modifier`,\n  agency→`agency`, pool→`poolNumber`, allocations→`allocations`).\n- Integer-cent allocation tolerance via `withinOneCent` (`calculations.ts:3-5`).\n- Lifecycle helpers preserve internal ID and append audit history; book throws\n  on errors; cancel throws unless booked; cancelled records stay visible.\n- Reducer covers all twelve contract actions, keeps `editingTradeId`, blocks\n  editing cancelled trades, keeps selection on the cancelled record, and takes\n  caller-supplied `{ id, at }` so it stays deterministic. Reducer and selectors\n  import no React.\n- Seed data: six trades, all six products, 3 booked / 1 validated / 1 draft /\n  1 cancelled, buys and sells, one warning, varied counterparties, books,\n  traders, factors, prices, modifiers, deep-frozen, all obviously synthetic,\n  `synthetic: true`.\n- Search across internal ID, client ID, security ID, deal, and counterparty,\n  case-insensitive; three sorts with internal-ID tie-break; product and status\n  filters (`state/selectors.ts`).\n- Accessibility contract in source: `tc-field-{field}` / `tc-error-{field}`\n  IDs, `aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby`, `role=\"status\"` live region,\n  disabled Book with visible reason, table caption, `role=\"region\"` +\n  `tabIndex={0}` + accessible name, `aria-pressed` row buttons,\n  `:focus-visible` outlines.\n- Every CSS selector begins with `.tc-`; no `:root`, bare element, or universal\n  selector; homepage asserted free of `tc-` markup\n  (`tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:51`).\n- No new dependencies, no network/storage/auth code, deterministic first render\n  (fixed empty-draft and seed timestamps; `Date.now`/`crypto.randomUUID` only\n  inside handlers; all `Intl` formatters pinned to `en-US`/UTC).\n- Implementation log labels Codex/Claude subscription telemetry separately from\n  metered OpenRouter spend, preserves the Terra and Sonnet failures with causes,\n  records the Kimi timeout as ungraded with zero files written, reattributes the\n  six workspace files to frontier implementation, discloses the generated hero\n  image, and records the browser-QA failure as an unverified gap.\n\n## Evidence limits\n\n- Nothing was executed. Typecheck, lint, build, the three suites,\n  `benchmark:validate`, and `npm run verify` are unverified by this review.\n- No browser was used. Rendered layout, focus visibility, contrast as painted,\n  console cleanliness, 390px behaviour, and page-level overflow remain\n  unverified — the same gap the implementation log already declares.\n- `benchmark/private` and `benchmark/runs` were not read, so the claim that the\n  four private Kimi workspace checks pass, the Sonnet blob hash `00720b0…`, the\n  Qwen blob `c91f316…`, and all elapsed/token/cost figures are unverified.\n- Git history, worktree cleanliness, and the claim that only preregistered\n  paths changed were not inspected (no commands run).\n- The contrast figures in finding 10 are computed from source hex values.\n- `public/trade-capture-structure.png` exists but its rendered appearance and\n  the legibility of hero text over it were not assessed.\n\n## Recommended next actions\n\n1. Guard lifecycle status regression: reject or explicitly model\n   booked → draft/validated in `domain/lifecycle.ts`, and add illegal-transition\n   tests alongside the existing book/cancel throw tests.\n2. Keep the ticket populated after `validate` (and after `save-draft`), clearing\n   only on `book` and `reset`, so fill → Validate → Book works in one pass and\n   Book no longer ends in a red error banner.\n3. Add touched/dirty tracking so a pristine ticket shows no errors and no\n   `aria-invalid`, and surface `editingTradeId` in the ticket heading so editing\n   an existing record is visible.\n4. Add required-date validation with new frozen exception codes, and move focus\n   to the review heading after cancel and to the ticket after \"Edit in ticket\".\n5. Extend `tests/trade-workspace.test.mjs` and the rendered-page assertions to\n   cover error association, `aria-pressed`, the labelled scroll region, reset,\n   the cancelled-edit guard, and the sort tie-breaker; then complete the\n   deferred browser QA at desktop and 390px.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5338,"cache_read_input_tokens":80895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5338},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0534d7a-1d7b-4a4f-b438-f153dd9a57ff","uuid":"018b5216-70c1-44ce-8811-76c4bfa77675","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:06:16.521Z","request_id":"req_011CeLg8JebeSnG2xLLz7upZ"}
