{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeLgCWFxf3UuxJbehKxM4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write is disabled in this session, so the review is delivered inline (this was a read-only review regardless — no files edited, no commands run, no network, and `benchmark/private` / `benchmark/runs` untouched).\n\n## Verdict\n\n`ACCEPT WITH FINDINGS` — the mock implements the frozen domain, state, and accessibility contracts faithfully and the implementation log is honest about model output, fallback, cost, and unverified browser QA, but the lifecycle lets a booked trade regress to draft and the validate/book actions clear the ticket in a way that makes the intended capture flow confusing and misreports success.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **high** — `app/trade-capture/domain/lifecycle.ts:37-43`, `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts:120-137`. Booked records can silently regress. `edit` accepts any non-cancelled trade, and `saveDraft`/`validateTradeRecord` accept any `existing` trade and unconditionally write `status: \"draft\"`/`\"validated\"`. Editing a booked trade and pressing Save draft moves it back to `draft`, drops it from `bookedTradeCount` (`domain/calculations.ts:34`), and makes it permanently uncancellable (`lifecycle.ts:53-56`). Only two transitions are guarded — book-with-errors and cancel-non-booked — and no test covers the downgrade.\n\n2. **high** — `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts:82-96` with `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx:48-62`. `storeTrade` resets `draft` to `emptyDraft()` and `editingTradeId` to `null` after `save-draft`, `validate`, and `book`. So (a) the natural fill → Validate → Book path is impossible: Validate empties the ticket and re-disables Book, forcing the user through blotter select → \"Edit in ticket\"; (b) immediately after a successful Book the `role=\"status\"` region flips to `Ticket needs attention · 8 errors`, because the freshly emptied draft fails validation. Success is announced as failure.\n\n3. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/state/reducer.ts:103`, `app/trade-capture/components/trade-ticket.tsx:73,99,137`. No touched/dirty tracking. `INITIAL_STATE.exceptions = validateTrade(initialDraft)` means the first paint of an untouched ticket shows a red banner and sets `aria-invalid=\"true\"` plus inline error text on eight fields the user has never visited. Live validation on change is contract-required; validating a pristine form is not.\n\n4. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/domain/validation.ts:39-41`, `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts:26-41`. `PRODUCT.md` rule 1 makes trade date and settlement date required, but no `required-trade-date`/`required-settlement-date` code exists and the only date rule is the ordering check, which is skipped when either value is empty. Both are clearable `type=\"date\"` inputs (`trade-ticket.tsx:215-230`), so a trade with no trade date books cleanly.\n\n5. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/components/trade-review.tsx:104-109`; no `useRef`, `useEffect`, or `.focus(` exists anywhere under `app/trade-capture`. `ARCHITECTURE-OPUS-REVIEW.md:60-61` requires focus to return to the review heading after cancelling; instead the activated \"Cancel trade\" button becomes `disabled` and focus drops to `<body>`. \"Edit in ticket\" also moves no focus, which matters at 390px where the populated ticket is off-screen above the review panel.\n\n6. **medium** — `app/trade-capture/domain/types.ts:133-141`, `app/trade-capture/trade-capture-app.tsx:54-62`. `editingTradeId` never reaches the UI: `TradeTicketProps` has no editing field and the heading always reads \"New trade\". Selection and editing can diverge — select A, press \"Edit in ticket\", click B's row — after which Book overwrites A while the review panel shows B, with no visible cue.\n\n7. **medium** — `tests/trade-workspace.test.mjs`, `tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:54-75`. The frozen accessibility contract (`CONTRACT.md:48-59`) is almost entirely unasserted: nothing checks `aria-describedby`/`aria-invalid` association, `aria-pressed`, the labelled focusable scroll region, or the disabled-Book reason, although `ARCHITECTURE-OPUS-REVIEW.md:77-82` asked for described-error assertions. State coverage omits `reset`, `save-draft` on an existing trade, the cancelled-edit guard, and the internal-ID tie-breaker (the sort test only re-sorts the output it received). No component-level render test exists; page checks are regex over server HTML.\n\n8. **low** — `benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/IMPLEMENTATION-LOG.md:139-146`. The declared final gate (`ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md:290-298`) ends with `npm run verify`, which also runs `benchmark:mcp:test`. The log reports typecheck, lint, `npm test`, `benchmark:validate`, and `git diff --check`, but not `npm run verify`. The \"11 public behavior/render checks\" figure does match the suites (2 + 6 + 3).\n\n9. **low** — `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css:18,654-666,830-900`. The table is pinned to `min-width: 1120px`, so at 390px all nine columns are reachable only by horizontal scrolling inside the region, with no stacked fallback. Separately `.tc-shell { overflow-x: clip }` suppresses page-level overflow rather than preventing it, so an overflow regression would be hidden from exactly the manual 390px check meant to catch it.\n\n10. **low** — `app/trade-capture/trade-capture.css:10,216-221,507-511,540-544`. `--tc-muted` (#68777b) on the #f2f5f1/#fffdf8 panels computes to roughly 4.2:1, under the 4.5:1 AA threshold for normal text, and is applied at 8–11px (`.tc-exception strong` 8px, `.tc-detail-grid dt` 9px, `.tc-audit-list span` 9px).\n\n11. **low** — `package.json:5-12`, `tsconfig.json`. `npm test` imports `.ts` modules from `.mjs` suites, which needs unflagged type stripping (Node ≥22.18), while `engines.node` allows `>=22.13.0`. `erasableSyntaxOnly` is unset, so a future `enum` or parameter property would pass typecheck and break the domain suite at runtime.\n\n## Contract coverage\n\n- Six stable product identifiers, all trade fields, and the `TradeDraft`/`Trade`/`DeskSummary` shapes match `ARCHITECTURE-SOL.md` (`domain/types.ts`).\n- `current face = original face × factor`, `gross principal = current face × price / 100`, signed exposure, desk totals excluding cancelled trades, `sellExposure` kept negative (`domain/calculations.ts`).\n- Validation rules 2–4 and 6–11, frozen exception codes, and the cross-field ownership map (settlement→`settlementDate`, modifier→`modifier`, agency→`agency`, pool→`poolNumber`, allocations→`allocations`).\n- Integer-cent allocation tolerance via `withinOneCent` (`calculations.ts:3-5`), with boundary tests at 50.01/50.02.\n- Lifecycle helpers preserve internal ID and append audit history; book throws on errors; cancel throws unless booked; cancelled records stay visible.\n- Reducer implements all twelve contract actions, holds `editingTradeId`, blocks editing cancelled trades, keeps selection on the cancelled record, and takes caller-supplied `{ id, at }`. Reducer and selectors import no React and are tested directly.\n- Seed: six trades, all six products, 3 booked / 1 validated / 1 draft / 1 cancelled, buys and sells, one warning, varied counterparties/books/traders/factors/prices/modifiers, deep-frozen, plainly synthetic, `synthetic: true`.\n- Search over internal ID, client ID, security ID, deal, counterparty, case-insensitive; three sorts with internal-ID tie-break; product and status filters.\n- Accessibility contract present in source: `tc-field-{field}`/`tc-error-{field}` IDs, `aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby`, `role=\"status\"` live region, disabled Book with visible reason, table caption, `role=\"region\"` + `tabIndex={0}` + accessible name, `aria-pressed` row buttons, `:focus-visible` outlines.\n- Every CSS selector begins with `.tc-`; no `:root`, bare element, or universal selector; the homepage is asserted free of `tc-` markup (`tests/rendered-html.test.mjs:51`).\n- No new dependencies, no network/storage/auth, deterministic first render — fixed empty-draft and seed timestamps, `Date.now`/`crypto.randomUUID` only inside handlers, all `Intl` formatters pinned to `en-US`/UTC.\n- The implementation log separates subscription telemetry from metered OpenRouter spend, preserves the Terra and Sonnet failures with causes, records the Kimi timeout as ungraded with zero files written, reattributes the six workspace files to frontier implementation, discloses the generated hero image, and records the browser-QA failure as an unverified gap rather than a pass.\n\n## Evidence limits\n\n- Nothing was executed. Typecheck, lint, build, the three suites, `benchmark:validate`, and `npm run verify` are unverified here.\n- No browser was used: rendered layout, focus visibility, painted contrast, console cleanliness, 390px behaviour, and page overflow remain unverified — the same gap the log declares.\n- `benchmark/private` and `benchmark/runs` were not read, so the four private Kimi checks, the Sonnet blob `00720b0…`, the Qwen blob `c91f316…`, and every elapsed/token/cost figure are unverified.\n- Git history and worktree cleanliness were not inspected, so \"only preregistered paths changed\" is unverified.\n- Finding 10's contrast ratios are computed from source hex values, not measured.\n- `public/trade-capture-structure.png` exists, but hero-text legibility over it was not assessed.\n\n## Recommended next actions\n\n1. Guard status regression in `domain/lifecycle.ts` (reject or explicitly model booked → draft/validated) and add illegal-transition tests beside the existing throw tests.\n2. Keep the ticket populated after `validate` and `save-draft`, clearing only on `book` and `reset`, so fill → Validate → Book works in one pass and Book no longer ends in a red error banner.\n3. Add touched/dirty tracking so a pristine ticket shows no errors or `aria-invalid`, and surface `editingTradeId` in the ticket heading.\n4. Add required trade-date/settlement-date validation with new frozen codes, and move focus to the review heading after cancel and to the ticket after \"Edit in ticket\".\n5. Extend the workspace and rendered-page tests to cover error association, `aria-pressed`, the labelled scroll region, reset, the cancelled-edit guard, and the sort tie-breaker; then complete the deferred browser QA at desktop and 390px."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4743,"cache_read_input_tokens":86233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4743},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0534d7a-1d7b-4a4f-b438-f153dd9a57ff","uuid":"d56bee80-7dbd-4dda-a025-970d34e38d49","timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:07:02.849Z","request_id":"req_011CeLgCUGALdZtfxCbLWXWq"}
